[41.363074, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b]2;yoloctl — ✳ leogr\\coder: @coder agent in #space\u0007\u001b[0 q\u001b[2;5H\u001b[38;2;217;119;87;1m✳\u001b[38;5;215m  leogr\\coder: @coder agent in #space ✕ \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[48;5;237m  \u001b[38;5;231mthe lead asks there for this project, without asking me. Answer in the \u001b[39m       \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[48;5;237m  \u001b[38;5;231mthread with airc send --reply; when you post the plan, include the link \u001b[39m      \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[48;5;237m  \u001b[38;5;231m[PLAN.md](PLAN.md). Work directly in this project folder, with no git \u001b[39m        \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[48;5;237m  \u001b[38;5;231mworktrees, and leave branch health checked out until the merge. Commit with \u001b[39m  \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[48;5;237m  \u001b[38;5;231mthe project's git identity and no co-author lines; you have no Go, the tester\u001b[39m \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[48;5;237m  \u001b[38;5;231mruns the tests; write the plan's diagram as a left-to-right flowchart \u001b[39m        \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[48;5;237m  \u001b[38;5;231m(flowchart LR) of exactly three boxes, each one short word (at most 6 \u001b[39m        \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[48;5;237m  \u001b[38;5;231mletters, like Plan, Code, Test), with no labels on the arrows and no quotes.\u001b[39m  \u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[38;5;114m●\u001b[m \u001b[1mSkill\u001b[m(airc)\r\n\u001b[38;5;246m  ⎿  \u001b[mLoaded skill\r\n\n  \u001b[38;5;246mRan \u001b[1m4\u001b[22m shell commands \u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[38;5;231m●\u001b[m I'm connected to #space as @coder. Nothing has been asked of me yet, and the\r\n  delivery monitor will wake me when someone mentions @coder.\r\n\n\u001b[38;5;246m✻\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;246mCooked for 20s · done 1:09 PM · 1 monitor still running\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[38;5;244m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n❯ \u001b[7m \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[38;5;244m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\n  \u001b[38;5;211m⏵⏵ bypass permissions on\u001b[38;5;246m · \u001b[38;5;44m1 monitor\u001b[38;5;246m · ↓ to manage\u001b[m"]
[41.379773, "o", "\r\u001b[5d\u001b[6L\u001b[3d\u001b[38;5;174m▝▜\u001b[48;5;16m█████\u001b[49m█▀\u001b[m  \u001b[38;5;246mOpus 5.5 · Claude Ultra\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[38;5;174m ▝▝   ▝▝ \u001b[m  \u001b[38;5;246m/workdir/var/tmp/demo040/project\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\n\u001b[38;5;220m⚠\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;220mYour login expires in 2 days\u001b[38;5;246m · run /login to renew\u001b[m\r\n\n  Fable 5.2 is here for your longest and toughest coding tasks. It draws down usage faster than Opus 5.5. Switch with\r\n  \u001b[38;5;153m/model\u001b[m.\r\n\n\u001b[38;5;246;48;5;237m❯ \u001b[38;5;231mYou are @coder in this team: listen for @coder in #space and do what leogr or the lead asks there for this project, \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\n\u001b[4G\u001b[38;5;231;48;5;237mithout asking me. Answer in the thread with airc send --reply; when you post the plan, include the link \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\n\u001b[3G\u001b[38;5;231;48;5;237m[PLAN.md](PLAN.md). Work directly in this project folder, with no git worktrees, and leave branch health checked out \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\n\u001b[3G\u001b[38;5;231;48;5;237muntil the merge. Commit with the project's git identity and no co-author lines; you have no Go, the tester runs the \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\n\u001b[3G\u001b[38;5;231;48;5;237mtests; write the plan's diagram as a left-to-right flowchart (flowchart LR) of exactly three boxes, each one short \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\n\u001b[3G\u001b[38;5;231;48;5;237mword (at most 6 letters, like Plan, Code, Test), with no labels on the arrows and no quotes.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\u001b[23;80Hdelivery monitor will wake me when\r\n  someone mentions @coder.\u001b[K\u001b[28;81H\u001b[38;5;244m────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\u001b[30;81H\u001b[38;5;244m────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m"]
